WEBVTT

00:32:28.540 --> 00:32:30.288
from white people to black people.

00:32:30.312 --> 00:32:32.417
I think it should be a sign of respect

00:32:32.441 --> 00:32:36.274
for all of the pain and suffering that has
been inflicted through discrimination,

00:32:36.298 --> 00:32:37.472
through slavery,

00:32:37.496 --> 00:32:41.286
and it should be a process
of coming together to figure this out.

00:32:41.310 --> 00:32:43.063
And as Coates writes in that essay,

00:32:43.087 --> 00:32:45.453
the very process of having
this conversation

00:32:45.477 --> 00:32:48.803
is a way to show the respect,
a way to acknowledge wounds,

00:32:48.827 --> 00:32:53.722
and a way to acknowledge that,
collectively, this has been our great sin.

00:32:53.746 --> 00:32:57.247
And it's the great radiating sin
that has polluted a lot of our society.

00:32:57.271 --> 00:32:58.870
And it's the sort of gesture

00:32:58.894 --> 00:33:01.708
that could at least get us
over to the other side,